1
00:00:00,340 --> 00:00:01,670
(All people, incidents,
and backgrounds...)

2
00:00:01,670 --> 00:00:03,440
(in this drama are fictitious
and unrelated to reality.)

3
00:00:03,440 --> 00:00:04,910
(Also, children were filmed
under production guidelines.)

4
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:07,710
(Episode 64)

5
00:00:11,550 --> 00:00:13,080
You all saw the news, right?

6
00:00:14,290 --> 00:00:15,290
Mom.

7
00:00:16,690 --> 00:00:19,860
Wait, how did you get here?

8
00:00:19,990 --> 00:00:22,660
I came with the person
who helped me.

9
00:00:23,030 --> 00:00:24,760
What do you mean,
the person who helped you?

10
00:00:25,730 --> 00:00:26,730
Come on in.

11
00:00:35,340 --> 00:00:36,340
Ko Eun Seol?

12
00:00:36,610 --> 00:00:39,510
Eun Seol helped me out
a lot this time.

13
00:00:48,090 --> 00:00:49,090
Yes, Director Joo.

14
00:00:50,860 --> 00:00:51,860
What's with that article?

15
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:55,530
Who ordered you
to write that garbage?

16
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:59,500
I figured this would be a good time
to update my client list.

17
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:01,570
What?

18
00:01:01,830 --> 00:01:03,270
Instead of serving
Cheongma's loyal dog,

19
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:06,540
staying close to the master
seems far more profitable.

20
00:01:07,440 --> 00:01:09,010
Hey, Do Ji Hoon!

21
00:01:11,610 --> 00:01:12,610
Darn it.

22
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:22,890
Wait, Ms. Ko went directly
to your ex-manager?

23
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:24,020
Yes.

24
00:01:24,260 --> 00:01:26,720
She cleared things up
with Manager An...

25
00:01:26,830 --> 00:01:29,460
and even asked the reporter
for a retraction.

26
00:01:30,030 --> 00:01:32,960
If it weren't for her,
things could've gone horribly wrong.

27
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:35,870
Honey, really.

28
00:01:36,530 --> 00:01:38,940
You owe her big time for this.

29
00:01:39,900 --> 00:01:40,940
I know.

30
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:44,080
And I plan on paying her back
for a long time.

31
00:01:45,640 --> 00:01:47,310
Ko Eun Seol works for Cheongma too.

32
00:01:47,680 --> 00:01:49,780
It's only natural for her
to help her superior in a bind.

33
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:53,050
Why are you overreacting
over nothing?

34
00:01:53,080 --> 00:01:55,220
Helping out
just because it's your job...

35
00:01:55,620 --> 00:01:57,820
and genuinely caring
are two different things.

36
00:01:58,960 --> 00:02:02,530
So going forward,
Eun Seol will be assisting me.

37
00:02:04,530 --> 00:02:06,560
Not as an official secretary,

38
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:09,770
but she'll be helping me out
with my day-to-day work.

39
00:02:10,570 --> 00:02:13,140
Hasn't Director Joo been handling
those things so far?

40
00:02:14,470 --> 00:02:15,740
Well, Director Joo...

41
00:02:17,640 --> 00:02:19,940
Isn't she stretched a bit too thin
these days?

42
00:02:21,310 --> 00:02:25,650
Eun Seol can cover
whatever Director Joo might miss.

43
00:02:27,350 --> 00:02:28,690
Don't you agree, Director Joo?

44
00:02:31,160 --> 00:02:32,990
Yes, of course.

45
00:02:33,890 --> 00:02:35,330
I'll do my very best...

46
00:02:35,590 --> 00:02:37,930
to support the Chairman
so you don't have to worry.

47
00:02:41,770 --> 00:02:44,870
Ko Eun Seol, how dare you
stab me in the back like this?

48
00:02:49,610 --> 00:02:50,610
What now?

49
00:02:51,110 --> 00:02:54,050
I already have enough on my plate
without Ko Eun Seol acting out too.

50
00:02:57,150 --> 00:02:59,680
You said to trust you.
You said you'd handle everything.

51
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:03,660
Stop it. Just stop. Let me think.

52
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,720
What's there to think about?

53
00:03:05,820 --> 00:03:06,820
Just get rid of Ko Eun Seol.

54
00:03:06,890 --> 00:03:08,060
Won't that solve everything?

55
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:10,160
Do you think it's that easy?

56
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:11,430
Do you really think...

57
00:03:11,600 --> 00:03:13,770
she'll just walk away
if we try to force her out?

58
00:03:14,330 --> 00:03:15,970
How can you still not know
what she's like?

59
00:03:17,070 --> 00:03:19,340
If you won't do it, I will.

60
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:20,840
You.

61
00:03:21,210 --> 00:03:22,240
Listen to me.

62
00:03:22,810 --> 00:03:24,080
Don't do anything rash.

63
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:26,540
Just focus on your work.

64
00:03:53,970 --> 00:03:56,210
Was the hotel comfortable?

65
00:03:58,880 --> 00:04:01,780
Yes, it was nice
to clear my head for once...

66
00:04:02,010 --> 00:04:03,510
and get some good rest.

67
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:06,820
Since when were you
so close to Ko Eun Seol?

68
00:04:07,820 --> 00:04:10,320
She's not exactly on the best terms
with Hae Ra.

69
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:11,960
Well, that was in the past.

70
00:04:12,390 --> 00:04:13,420
These days,

71
00:04:13,490 --> 00:04:16,830
Eun Seol actually helps Hae Ra out
quite a lot.

72
00:04:17,160 --> 00:04:18,160
Is that so?

73
00:04:20,770 --> 00:04:23,030
How were things with you?

74
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:25,940
What do you mean?

75
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:29,740
How were you while I was away?

76
00:04:30,270 --> 00:04:31,380
Did anything happen?

77
00:04:31,710 --> 00:04:34,850
Well, it felt empty and lonely
without you.

78
00:04:35,810 --> 00:04:36,810
Did it?

79
00:04:39,980 --> 00:04:42,720
That's 50, 51, 52.

80
00:04:45,820 --> 00:04:46,860
Then 60, 61...

81
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:49,060
- What are you doing?
- Hey, you're back.

82
00:04:49,360 --> 00:04:50,430
What's all that money?

83
00:04:50,700 --> 00:04:53,200
Well, turns out
she has some decency.

84
00:04:53,870 --> 00:04:56,800
If I'd known she'd be so generous,

85
00:04:57,370 --> 00:04:59,600
I would've treated
our freeloader better.

86
00:04:59,740 --> 00:05:00,770
By the way, Eun Seol,

87
00:05:01,340 --> 00:05:04,310
is it really okay for us
to keep this money?

88
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,110
I mean, this note...

89
00:05:06,840 --> 00:05:09,250
makes it pretty clear
she left it for us.

90
00:05:13,280 --> 00:05:14,720
(I'm sorry for the trouble,
and thank you. From Kim Jung Sun)

91
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:18,960
We should probably return it, right?

92
00:05:20,430 --> 00:05:21,430
No.

93
00:05:21,990 --> 00:05:24,500
Chairman Kim gave it
to you and Grandma.

94
00:05:24,900 --> 00:05:27,000
- You can keep it.
- Of course we're keeping it.

95
00:05:27,070 --> 00:05:28,270
Why on earth would we give it back?

96
00:05:28,430 --> 00:05:30,030
All she's got is money
to throw around.

97
00:05:30,100 --> 00:05:32,840
- I'll get some rest.
- Sure, go ahead and rest.

98
00:05:36,040 --> 00:05:39,540
Maybe we should start
running a boarding house.

99
00:05:39,610 --> 00:05:41,710
Who runs a boarding house
these days?

100
00:05:42,280 --> 00:05:44,720
People call them GH now.

101
00:05:44,850 --> 00:05:46,820
A guesthouse, they call it.

102
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:49,250
A GH? Guest what?

103
00:05:50,250 --> 00:05:52,820
A guesthouse. And with guesthouses,

104
00:05:52,890 --> 00:05:54,760
serving breakfast is standard.

105
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:57,430
Mom, could you cook breakfast
every single morning?

106
00:05:58,300 --> 00:05:59,900
Over my dead body.

107
00:06:00,260 --> 00:06:03,400
Then forget about it.

108
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:04,670
Fine.

109
00:06:04,870 --> 00:06:06,400
Let's just keep living
the way we do.

110
00:06:06,670 --> 00:06:08,810
(Eun Seol, thanks for everything.
I saw this and thought of you.)

111
00:06:12,780 --> 00:06:15,610
Eun Seol, thanks for everything.

112
00:06:16,380 --> 00:06:18,650
I saw this and thought of you.

113
00:06:32,760 --> 00:06:33,770
So pretty.

114
00:07:21,610 --> 00:07:24,150
Aren't you pushing yourself too hard
right after getting back?

115
00:07:24,550 --> 00:07:26,480
You could've rested a bit longer.

116
00:07:27,050 --> 00:07:30,190
Rest? I need to work
even harder now.

117
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:33,930
That's the only way
I can avoid any accusations...

118
00:07:33,990 --> 00:07:35,560
of abusing my power.

119
00:07:35,730 --> 00:07:37,630
You're already doing
more than enough.

120
00:07:37,700 --> 00:07:41,030
That kind of complacent advice
is exactly what puts me in danger.

121
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:46,740
Why do you have to be
so negative about it?

122
00:07:46,970 --> 00:07:49,770
Director Joo's only saying that
out of concern for you.

123
00:07:51,380 --> 00:07:54,010
What I need right now
isn't flattery,

124
00:07:54,550 --> 00:07:57,180
it's practical solutions.

125
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:59,450
Neither you nor Director Joo...

126
00:07:59,520 --> 00:08:02,420
will suffer the humiliation
in my place.

127
00:08:02,420 --> 00:08:03,920
Just as this incident proved.

128
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:06,860
So,

129
00:08:07,460 --> 00:08:09,830
I'd appreciate it if you didn't...

130
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:13,160
cloud my judgment with sweet talk.

131
00:08:14,400 --> 00:08:17,030
Do you understand what I'm saying,
Director Joo?

132
00:08:26,080 --> 00:08:28,280
Has everything been all right
while I was away?

133
00:08:28,910 --> 00:08:30,050
Yes, everything's been fine.

134
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:33,280
I should have reached out sooner
and come to see you. I'm sorry.

135
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:34,950
Gosh, don't be.

136
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,220
You reached out
right after the article dropped.

137
00:08:37,920 --> 00:08:40,560
I was truly grateful for that.

138
00:08:42,260 --> 00:08:44,660
This whole incident taught me a lot.

139
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:47,770
I'm only telling you
and Hae Ra this,

140
00:08:49,370 --> 00:08:50,500
but the truth is,

141
00:08:50,870 --> 00:08:54,140
I've been staying
at Eun Seol's place all this time.

142
00:08:54,970 --> 00:08:56,240
Ko Eun Seol's place?

143
00:08:56,670 --> 00:08:57,680
Yes.

144
00:08:58,240 --> 00:08:59,680
Strange, isn't it?

145
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:03,250
For some reason,
right from the start,

146
00:09:03,410 --> 00:09:05,920
I just felt drawn to her.

147
00:09:06,920 --> 00:09:09,890
If it hadn't been for Eun Seol
through all this,

148
00:09:10,320 --> 00:09:12,990
I never would've made it back
this quickly.

149
00:09:13,620 --> 00:09:14,630
By the way,

150
00:09:15,260 --> 00:09:17,090
how is So Yeon doing?

151
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:18,630
She's gotten a lot better,

152
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:20,300
though some things never change.

153
00:09:20,800 --> 00:09:21,930
Speaking of which,

154
00:09:22,100 --> 00:09:24,240
should we all grab a meal
with So Yeon?

155
00:09:25,640 --> 00:09:28,170
Spending time together
helps people bond, after all.

156
00:09:29,340 --> 00:09:30,340
Yes, sounds great.

157
00:09:31,410 --> 00:09:33,580
You startled me yesterday.

158
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:36,710
I never expected you to walk in
with the Chairman like that.

159
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,180
I bet you were totally surprised.

160
00:09:41,350 --> 00:09:42,350
A little.

161
00:09:43,690 --> 00:09:46,420
Helping the Chairman
is helping you, Mom.

162
00:09:47,330 --> 00:09:48,930
And I thought
if I worked hard to help her,

163
00:09:49,090 --> 00:09:51,500
we could bring the Chairman over
to our side.

164
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,760
True.

165
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:55,530
Still,

166
00:09:56,300 --> 00:09:58,940
why are you working so hard
all of a sudden?

167
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,400
You weren't like this before.

168
00:10:00,670 --> 00:10:02,640
I've started setting my sights
on Cheongma.

169
00:10:04,380 --> 00:10:06,340
I'm allowed to dream, aren't I?

170
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:08,550
A dream of owning Cheongma.

171
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:13,080
Well, you're certainly allowed
to want that.

172
00:10:13,920 --> 00:10:16,550
I want to help you
and the Chairman even more...

173
00:10:17,050 --> 00:10:18,890
so I can climb higher.

174
00:10:19,390 --> 00:10:21,460
All the way up the ladder
at Cheongma.

175
00:10:24,030 --> 00:10:27,060
I never knew my daughter
was so ambitious.

176
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:29,470
I take after you, Mom.

177
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:36,340
Dinner together all of a sudden?

178
00:10:37,040 --> 00:10:38,480
Isn't this a bit out of nowhere?

179
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:41,550
She just wants us to share a meal
to celebrate her return.

180
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:43,880
She was only gone for a few days.

181
00:10:44,220 --> 00:10:46,420
I'll pick up my mother later
and head straight to the restaurant.

182
00:10:47,020 --> 00:10:48,150
All right.

183
00:10:52,390 --> 00:10:55,690
Sounds like my dad really enjoyed
golfing with you over the weekend.

184
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:58,560
Looks like you scored
some major points with him.

185
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,460
Really? That's a relief.

186
00:11:03,400 --> 00:11:05,800
The CEO likes whiskey, right?

187
00:11:06,800 --> 00:11:08,510
Maybe I should take him out
to a bar next time.

188
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,040
Actually,

189
00:11:11,410 --> 00:11:13,580
my dad likes makgeolli
way more than whiskey.

190
00:11:14,580 --> 00:11:15,950
- Makgeolli?
- Yes.

191
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:18,820
When I was young,
I saw him drinking it all the time.

192
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:20,680
These days,

193
00:11:21,090 --> 00:11:22,790
no matter how high-end
the whiskey is,

194
00:11:22,850 --> 00:11:24,520
he doesn't enjoy it
as much as makgeolli.

195
00:11:25,520 --> 00:11:27,320
You know
my dad grew up working-class.

196
00:11:27,930 --> 00:11:30,530
I'll have to bring him
a bottle of makgeolli then.

197
00:11:31,030 --> 00:11:33,700
Mom and Director Joo have
a foundation meeting tomorrow.

198
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:36,070
Do you want to come by tomorrow?

199
00:11:36,470 --> 00:11:37,570
Sure, sounds good.

200
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:46,840
Good morning, sir.

201
00:11:47,710 --> 00:11:50,350
Ms. Ko, are you headed somewhere?

202
00:11:50,850 --> 00:11:52,450
I have a meeting
for the scholarship program.

203
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:53,620
Is that so?

204
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:56,450
Now that the Chairman is back,
you must be busy.

205
00:11:57,320 --> 00:11:58,360
Don't let me keep you.

206
00:11:58,690 --> 00:11:59,690
Then...

207
00:12:01,930 --> 00:12:02,960
Ms. Ko.

208
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:09,670
If you ever need to help
the Chairman in the future,

209
00:12:10,330 --> 00:12:11,970
let me know beforehand.

210
00:12:13,340 --> 00:12:14,340
Pardon?

211
00:12:14,440 --> 00:12:15,840
Feel free to reach out anytime.

212
00:12:17,140 --> 00:12:18,140
No need to hesitate.

213
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,750
Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

214
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:28,290
(An Guk Cheol)

215
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:36,360
Hae Ra, it's Dad.

216
00:12:37,030 --> 00:12:39,430
I'll wait until you get off work.

217
00:12:39,760 --> 00:12:40,760
Call me.

218
00:12:43,230 --> 00:12:44,770
"Dad," my foot.

219
00:12:53,010 --> 00:12:54,010
Understood.

220
00:13:01,550 --> 00:13:05,320
(An Guk Cheol)

221
00:13:19,470 --> 00:13:20,600
What's this piece of trash?

222
00:13:21,370 --> 00:13:23,770
Come on. What are you calling trash?

223
00:13:24,210 --> 00:13:26,710
It's my first gift to my princess.

224
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:31,080
Instead of picking this stuff out,

225
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:33,220
figure out a way
to get rid of Ko Eun Seol.

226
00:13:33,750 --> 00:13:34,750
Right, sure.

227
00:13:35,490 --> 00:13:37,050
We have to take her down first.

228
00:13:38,360 --> 00:13:39,990
You said you'd do anything
for me, right?

229
00:13:41,960 --> 00:13:43,790
Then do whatever it takes...

230
00:13:43,860 --> 00:13:45,700
to get Ko Eun Seol
kicked out of Cheongma.

231
00:13:45,800 --> 00:13:48,430
Stuff like that
is right up my alley.

232
00:13:48,500 --> 00:13:50,530
Messing with people
and backstabbing them?

233
00:13:50,800 --> 00:13:52,770
I'm practically a pro.

234
00:13:54,070 --> 00:13:55,310
Can I really trust you?

235
00:13:55,440 --> 00:13:57,040
Of course you can.

236
00:13:58,010 --> 00:14:01,080
I'm your father. I can do it.

237
00:14:01,150 --> 00:14:02,150
Yes, I can!

238
00:14:03,480 --> 00:14:04,550
Cut it out.

239
00:14:04,950 --> 00:14:06,580
Get home safe, sweetie.

240
00:14:17,860 --> 00:14:19,600
- Uncle.
- Hey.

241
00:14:20,830 --> 00:14:21,970
You made it.

242
00:14:22,700 --> 00:14:23,770
Come in for some tea.

243
00:14:23,770 --> 00:14:26,040
No, I need to get back right away.

244
00:14:26,040 --> 00:14:27,540
I'm swamped with rice cake orders.

245
00:14:27,610 --> 00:14:30,510
Since you came all this way,
just give me ten minutes.

246
00:14:32,080 --> 00:14:33,380
All right, why not?

247
00:14:33,740 --> 00:14:34,750
Let's go.

248
00:14:52,300 --> 00:14:53,300
Uncle.

249
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,600
Yes?

250
00:14:56,670 --> 00:14:57,740
This way.

251
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:10,110
Logan must be thrilled. Here you go.

252
00:15:11,150 --> 00:15:12,450
Right, of course.

253
00:15:13,720 --> 00:15:15,720
Uncle, is something wrong?

254
00:15:16,150 --> 00:15:17,220
Seok Jin.

255
00:15:18,090 --> 00:15:20,060
Remember that man
you ran into earlier?

256
00:15:20,590 --> 00:15:22,560
What's his name?

257
00:15:23,990 --> 00:15:25,260
He's Managing Director Oh Tae Seop.

258
00:15:25,260 --> 00:15:27,530
Right. He's Oh Tae Seop, isn't he?

259
00:15:28,770 --> 00:15:31,970
He's the one responsible
for your father's accident.

260
00:15:32,970 --> 00:15:35,540
I might be getting old
and forgetful,

261
00:15:35,710 --> 00:15:38,040
but my memory of him
is crystal clear.

262
00:15:39,410 --> 00:15:41,850
He apologized through an insurer.

263
00:15:42,250 --> 00:15:44,010
Talk about shameless.

264
00:15:45,220 --> 00:15:47,420
But how is he working here?

265
00:15:47,790 --> 00:15:50,690
How did
a low-level delivery driver...

266
00:15:50,890 --> 00:15:53,090
ever become a managing director?

267
00:15:56,330 --> 00:15:57,560
What kind of settlement
did they reach...

268
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:59,930
for him to kill a man
and live so comfortably?

269
00:16:02,230 --> 00:16:04,300
My poor brother-in-law is
the only real victim in all this.

270
00:16:12,310 --> 00:16:16,950
So Yeon, try some of this.
It's seasoned just right.

271
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:18,680
Thank you.

272
00:16:23,790 --> 00:16:24,820
Hae Ra,

273
00:16:25,420 --> 00:16:28,360
you should have some too.

274
00:16:29,090 --> 00:16:32,800
Pumpkin is great
for reducing swelling.

275
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:37,700
It's time you looked pretty, too.

276
00:16:42,610 --> 00:16:45,110
Mother, I'm already pretty.

277
00:16:45,410 --> 00:16:48,180
Besides, I don't have
any swelling at all.

278
00:16:48,250 --> 00:16:52,050
No, you look puffy to me
all the time.

279
00:16:54,790 --> 00:16:57,860
Well, pumpkin sure is great
for reducing swelling.

280
00:16:58,420 --> 00:17:01,590
We're having a good laugh
thanks to you, So Yeon.

281
00:17:03,790 --> 00:17:06,100
Laughing over
what a sick person said?

282
00:17:06,530 --> 00:17:07,830
That's rude of you.

283
00:17:09,730 --> 00:17:11,840
I'm sorry, So Yeon.

284
00:17:12,470 --> 00:17:13,940
That was careless of me.

285
00:17:21,710 --> 00:17:23,010
What kind of settlement
did they reach...

286
00:17:23,080 --> 00:17:25,480
for him to kill a man
and live so comfortably?

287
00:17:35,830 --> 00:17:37,060
Excuse me, sir.

288
00:17:37,530 --> 00:17:38,530
Yes?

289
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:40,500
By any chance,

290
00:17:41,270 --> 00:17:43,530
do you know anything
about my father's...

291
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:45,640
accident settlement?

292
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,710
The accident settlement?

293
00:17:53,210 --> 00:17:56,410
Yes. They said a friend drafted it,

294
00:17:57,250 --> 00:18:00,620
and I heard you were the one
who handled the aftermath.

295
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:04,290
Right.

296
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,490
Well, I...

297
00:18:07,490 --> 00:18:08,730
That's right.

298
00:18:09,090 --> 00:18:13,300
Hae Ra's dad filled in
that settlement thing for me.

299
00:18:24,740 --> 00:18:27,340
You even took care of that for them?

300
00:18:30,480 --> 00:18:33,820
Well, you and Seong Woo
were really close.

301
00:18:33,880 --> 00:18:36,250
Dad, I guess you really were close
with Seok Jin's dad.

302
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:43,430
Mother.

303
00:18:44,090 --> 00:18:46,100
Why are you suddenly
covering your mouth?

304
00:18:47,660 --> 00:18:49,630
- Take your hands away.
- No, I can't.

305
00:18:49,900 --> 00:18:51,840
I won't say another word.

306
00:18:52,700 --> 00:18:54,710
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

307
00:18:54,710 --> 00:18:55,710
Mom?

308
00:18:56,370 --> 00:18:57,640
What's gotten into you?

309
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,510
- Take your hands away.
- I can't.

310
00:19:03,450 --> 00:19:05,520
I won't say anything.

311
00:19:06,150 --> 00:19:08,790
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

312
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,520
Mom?

313
00:19:11,690 --> 00:19:13,490
So Yeon, what's wrong?

314
00:19:13,690 --> 00:19:15,190
Are you not feeling well?

315
00:19:15,390 --> 00:19:17,390
What's happening?
What's wrong with her?

316
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,960
Let's wrap up dinner here.

317
00:19:21,730 --> 00:19:23,430
So Yeon doesn't look well.

318
00:19:23,730 --> 00:19:25,170
We should, Chief Cha.

319
00:19:25,470 --> 00:19:27,600
Take So Yeon home right away.

320
00:19:28,410 --> 00:19:29,770
Right, I'm sorry about this.

321
00:19:29,970 --> 00:19:32,640
- We'll get going then.
- Yes, go ahead.

322
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:35,110
I'm sorry.

323
00:19:35,450 --> 00:19:37,110
- I'm so sorry.
- Please excuse us.

324
00:19:37,410 --> 00:19:38,450
Oh no.

325
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:54,260
Whatever you heard,
you'd better keep your mouth shut.

326
00:19:55,430 --> 00:19:57,370
If you dare to run your mouth,

327
00:19:58,540 --> 00:20:00,870
your son won't be safe either.

328
00:20:02,340 --> 00:20:03,440
Understand?

329
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:12,320
Is that why you covered your mouth
and put on that little show?

330
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:25,160
Hae Ra's dad filled in
that settlement thing for me.

331
00:20:30,430 --> 00:20:33,140
Whatever you heard,
you'd better keep your mouth shut.

332
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:35,510
If you dare to run your mouth,

333
00:20:35,940 --> 00:20:37,980
your son won't be safe either.

334
00:21:20,080 --> 00:21:21,790
- Mr. Seok Jin.
- Yes?

335
00:21:21,790 --> 00:21:24,020
- Drink this before heading to work.
- Sure.

336
00:21:25,060 --> 00:21:26,590
What are you doing, though?

337
00:21:26,690 --> 00:21:28,090
I'm looking for something.

338
00:21:28,690 --> 00:21:32,460
Mom, where's the accident settlement
with the driver?

339
00:21:32,630 --> 00:21:34,060
What? I...

340
00:21:34,300 --> 00:21:36,470
I don't know.

341
00:21:36,800 --> 00:21:38,040
I really don't know.

342
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:40,670
Mom, try hard to remember.
I need that.

343
00:21:40,870 --> 00:21:42,340
We really need that document.

344
00:21:42,470 --> 00:21:43,810
I have to find it.

345
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:47,010
Well, that...

346
00:21:47,540 --> 00:21:50,350
Hae Ra's dad took all of it.

347
00:21:51,420 --> 00:21:52,450
The CEO?

348
00:21:53,180 --> 00:21:56,090
I heard him that day.

349
00:21:57,090 --> 00:21:58,560
Hae Ra's dad told that man...

350
00:21:59,420 --> 00:22:01,190
he did a good job.

351
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:05,230
To the person who hurt my husband...

352
00:22:06,300 --> 00:22:10,070
He thanked him
for killing my darling.

353
00:22:11,740 --> 00:22:12,770
What?

354
00:22:16,640 --> 00:22:20,110
No, I can't tell Mr. Seok Jin this.

355
00:22:21,010 --> 00:22:25,280
If I tell Mr. Seok Jin, he'd also...

356
00:22:26,450 --> 00:22:29,150
Tell me straight.
What do you mean by that?

357
00:22:29,690 --> 00:22:33,220
No.. No! My head hurts.

358
00:22:33,860 --> 00:22:35,590
My head hurts!

359
00:22:35,590 --> 00:22:36,590
Mom?

360
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:39,230
- My head!
- Are you okay?

361
00:22:39,800 --> 00:22:42,070
- Mom?
- It hurts!

362
00:22:44,500 --> 00:22:48,270
Don't worry about her
and just go to work.

363
00:22:48,970 --> 00:22:51,780
The doctor said
confusion over memories...

364
00:22:52,210 --> 00:22:53,810
is very common.

365
00:23:01,280 --> 00:23:03,520
Seok Jin, are you coming over today?

366
00:23:03,790 --> 00:23:06,020
You promised to have makgeolli
with my dad.

367
00:23:07,990 --> 00:23:10,430
Sure, let's go together after work.

368
00:23:14,970 --> 00:23:17,630
Have you been meeting up
with An Guk Cheol?

369
00:23:18,970 --> 00:23:20,900
What's wrong? Shouldn't I?

370
00:23:21,270 --> 00:23:23,210
Why do you keep
getting involved with him?

371
00:23:23,270 --> 00:23:24,780
I told you to cut him off.

372
00:23:25,210 --> 00:23:26,480
I want to, too.

373
00:23:26,640 --> 00:23:28,880
He keeps clinging to me,
so what am I supposed to do?

374
00:23:29,410 --> 00:23:30,680
You can't even cut him off?

375
00:23:32,550 --> 00:23:34,850
Who got involved with someone like that
in the first place?

376
00:23:37,590 --> 00:23:38,690
This won't do.

377
00:23:39,220 --> 00:23:41,490
I'll get An Guk Cheol thrown into
a psychiatric ward.

378
00:23:42,260 --> 00:23:43,260
What?

379
00:23:43,530 --> 00:23:45,430
That way,
you'll finally come to your senses.

380
00:23:45,860 --> 00:23:47,060
Didn't I tell you?

381
00:23:47,200 --> 00:23:48,830
This is the most critical time
for you right now.

382
00:23:48,970 --> 00:23:51,000
You can't afford
to get distracted like this.

383
00:23:51,540 --> 00:23:53,100
Don't send him away.

384
00:23:55,410 --> 00:23:56,570
I gave him a job to do.

385
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:59,180
A job? What kind of job?

386
00:24:00,310 --> 00:24:01,380
You don't need to know.

387
00:24:01,610 --> 00:24:03,110
I'll tell you
as soon as it's all handled.

388
00:24:11,390 --> 00:24:12,990
Seriously, that scumbag.

389
00:24:19,530 --> 00:24:20,560
It's me.

390
00:24:28,670 --> 00:24:30,610
The person you are trying to reach
is unavailable.

391
00:24:30,710 --> 00:24:31,710
Please try again later.

392
00:24:31,710 --> 00:24:34,140
You dare block me?

393
00:24:37,150 --> 00:24:38,650
Unbelievable.

394
00:24:38,750 --> 00:24:39,820
Ae Sook.

395
00:24:40,350 --> 00:24:42,990
Why on earth
would I answer your call?

396
00:24:43,390 --> 00:24:45,590
I have our princess now.

397
00:24:46,790 --> 00:24:49,660
Ae Sook, seriously.

398
00:24:49,790 --> 00:24:52,100
Yes, just like that!

399
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:54,030
Nice.

400
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:57,830
My grandma and dad told me
to make sure to thank you.

401
00:24:58,340 --> 00:25:00,640
I just did what anyone would do.

402
00:25:00,970 --> 00:25:04,170
Taking in a complete stranger
is never easy,

403
00:25:04,240 --> 00:25:07,580
especially when I'm the owner
of the company you work for.

404
00:25:08,410 --> 00:25:11,580
I'm sure they felt
very uncomfortable because of me.

405
00:25:12,280 --> 00:25:13,350
Not at all.

406
00:25:13,380 --> 00:25:18,020
My dad even kept the cup you used,
saying it's a souvenir.

407
00:25:21,790 --> 00:25:22,790
And...

408
00:25:23,560 --> 00:25:27,260
thank you so much for this.
It's so pretty.

409
00:25:28,270 --> 00:25:30,870
Eun Seol, ta-da.

410
00:25:31,470 --> 00:25:36,270
Actually, I got this
so we could match.

411
00:25:36,970 --> 00:25:38,140
Really?

412
00:25:39,510 --> 00:25:41,510
I wonder if Hae Ra
will feel left out.

413
00:25:42,410 --> 00:25:43,950
I should buy one for her, too.

414
00:25:47,550 --> 00:25:48,590
Hae Ra...

415
00:25:49,350 --> 00:25:50,520
must be so happy...

416
00:25:51,660 --> 00:25:53,590
to have a mother like you, ma'am.

417
00:25:55,060 --> 00:25:58,530
I honestly envy your mother,
Eun Seol,

418
00:25:59,060 --> 00:26:01,630
for having such a strong...

419
00:26:02,030 --> 00:26:03,700
and warm daughter like you.

420
00:26:04,670 --> 00:26:06,300
If she were still alive,

421
00:26:06,500 --> 00:26:09,570
I know she'd be
incredibly proud of you.

422
00:26:15,450 --> 00:26:16,480
We're closed.

423
00:26:18,650 --> 00:26:19,720
I don't think so.

424
00:26:20,420 --> 00:26:21,480
We're just getting started.

425
00:26:22,090 --> 00:26:23,190
Hey, Eun Seol.

426
00:26:23,450 --> 00:26:25,620
Great timing.
I was craving a beer anyway.

427
00:26:25,920 --> 00:26:26,990
Great minds think alike.

428
00:26:28,330 --> 00:26:30,360
Have a seat here. Just a moment.

429
00:26:39,040 --> 00:26:40,100
Did you come straight from work?

430
00:26:40,440 --> 00:26:44,110
Yes. Mi Rae told me I could drop by
whenever I wanted a beer.

431
00:26:45,310 --> 00:26:48,610
- Right?
- Of course. I love having you here.

432
00:26:50,880 --> 00:26:52,180
Cheers.

433
00:26:58,990 --> 00:27:01,090
Honestly, I was a little surprised.

434
00:27:02,460 --> 00:27:06,030
I had no idea the two of you
felt that way about each other.

435
00:27:06,900 --> 00:27:10,330
Since when did you two
get that close behind my back?

436
00:27:10,730 --> 00:27:12,570
You know that
once my mind's made up,

437
00:27:12,640 --> 00:27:15,240
I waste zero time
getting things moving.

438
00:27:15,670 --> 00:27:17,540
You could learn a thing or two
from my drive.

439
00:27:17,940 --> 00:27:19,340
I was more curious
about how she felt...

440
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:21,040
than in what you decided.

441
00:27:23,680 --> 00:27:24,810
To be honest,

442
00:27:26,180 --> 00:27:29,150
I accepted Eun Guk's feelings
because I owe it to Hyun Jae.

443
00:27:31,220 --> 00:27:35,060
Hyun Jae was rooting for us
until the day he died.

444
00:27:36,090 --> 00:27:37,630
It wasn't just about Eun Guk.

445
00:27:38,230 --> 00:27:39,230
You know how it is.

446
00:27:40,800 --> 00:27:44,300
Hyun Jae would've supported me
no matter what I decided.

447
00:27:45,700 --> 00:27:46,700
That's true.

448
00:27:47,970 --> 00:27:49,440
Attorney Seo would've done that.

449
00:27:50,710 --> 00:27:53,910
I guess Hyun Jae thought
I needed Eun Guk in my life.

450
00:27:54,380 --> 00:27:56,510
So, even though
it might seem selfish,

451
00:27:57,650 --> 00:27:59,450
I accepted Eun Guk's feelings.

452
00:28:00,780 --> 00:28:01,820
Or rather,

453
00:28:02,490 --> 00:28:04,050
I opened my heart.

454
00:28:04,390 --> 00:28:07,190
Turns out Attorney Seo helped me
until the very end.

455
00:28:08,890 --> 00:28:09,990
I had no idea...

456
00:28:10,290 --> 00:28:11,930
he was supportive of us.

457
00:28:12,830 --> 00:28:16,400
Exactly, so from now on,
treat me even better.

458
00:28:17,370 --> 00:28:20,040
Because Hyun Jae will be
watching over us from up there.

459
00:28:24,670 --> 00:28:25,680
Here.

460
00:28:25,980 --> 00:28:26,980
Cheers.

461
00:28:30,080 --> 00:28:31,310
- Let me pour you one, sir.
- Sure.

462
00:28:34,720 --> 00:28:36,090
- Here, have a drink too.
- Thank you.

463
00:28:38,790 --> 00:28:40,420
All right, let's drink.

464
00:28:46,660 --> 00:28:49,600
It's so good having this again
after so long.

465
00:28:50,600 --> 00:28:53,700
Yes, I definitely missed this.

466
00:28:53,840 --> 00:28:56,540
Strange, isn't it?

467
00:28:56,540 --> 00:28:58,910
- It is, sir.
- Chief Cha, people may change,

468
00:28:59,140 --> 00:29:01,580
- but this taste never changes.
- Indeed.

469
00:29:03,810 --> 00:29:08,220
So, how is So Yeon doing?
Did she go see a doctor?

470
00:29:08,520 --> 00:29:10,290
Yes. She's gotten better.

471
00:29:10,850 --> 00:29:12,320
Right, good.

472
00:29:14,490 --> 00:29:15,660
You didn't come here today...

473
00:29:15,660 --> 00:29:18,060
because you had something
to tell me, did you?

474
00:29:18,900 --> 00:29:21,100
I didn't have anything specific
to bring up.

475
00:29:21,160 --> 00:29:23,630
I just wanted to talk to you, sir.

476
00:29:24,270 --> 00:29:25,400
Talk about what?

477
00:29:26,400 --> 00:29:28,540
We could have talked at the office.

478
00:29:28,610 --> 00:29:29,640
Isn't it obvious?

479
00:29:30,110 --> 00:29:31,540
After leaving like that
the other day,

480
00:29:31,710 --> 00:29:33,010
he's trying to score points
with you.

481
00:29:34,680 --> 00:29:37,350
I was curious
about your life story, sir.

482
00:29:37,950 --> 00:29:40,150
If I'm to follow in your footsteps,

483
00:29:40,550 --> 00:29:43,350
your life experience will be
a great lesson for me.

484
00:29:44,190 --> 00:29:45,390
Follow in my footsteps?

485
00:29:46,460 --> 00:29:47,620
Well, pour me another.

486
00:29:50,630 --> 00:29:52,500
Here, let me pour you a drink too.

487
00:29:52,500 --> 00:29:53,700
- Please enjoy.
- Here.

488
00:29:53,700 --> 00:29:55,830
- Thank you, sir.
- All right, cheers.

489
00:29:56,070 --> 00:29:57,070
Cheers.

490
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:05,240
I'm getting sleepy.

491
00:30:05,410 --> 00:30:06,610
I think I'll go on up to bed.

492
00:30:06,680 --> 00:30:09,450
Yes, all right. Go on up, Hae Ra.

493
00:30:09,980 --> 00:30:11,080
Get some rest.

494
00:30:11,550 --> 00:30:14,080
Dad, you're completely hammered.
That's enough.

495
00:30:14,380 --> 00:30:17,890
All right.
I can handle myself, okay?

496
00:30:20,160 --> 00:30:23,630
- Well, let me pour you another.
- Right, sure.

497
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:26,930
It's overflowing.

498
00:30:33,640 --> 00:30:36,010
Spending time like this
with you, Chief Cha,

499
00:30:37,210 --> 00:30:39,480
brings back old memories.

500
00:30:42,850 --> 00:30:44,710
Back in the day,

501
00:30:45,250 --> 00:30:46,550
after work,

502
00:30:47,120 --> 00:30:50,220
Seong Woo and I would always go
for a drink before heading home.

503
00:30:51,920 --> 00:30:55,730
That was our only joy in life.

504
00:30:56,960 --> 00:30:57,960
I see.

505
00:31:04,900 --> 00:31:06,040
Man...

506
00:31:07,240 --> 00:31:11,910
Still, those were good times.

507
00:31:15,010 --> 00:31:18,250
What kind of man was my father?

508
00:31:19,020 --> 00:31:21,850
What? Who? Seong Woo?

509
00:31:24,750 --> 00:31:25,920
Seong Woo...

510
00:31:27,090 --> 00:31:28,590
He was meticulous...

511
00:31:29,490 --> 00:31:31,090
and diligent.

512
00:31:34,300 --> 00:31:37,130
But that meticulousness was
his downfall.

513
00:31:39,170 --> 00:31:40,200
That's...

514
00:31:40,770 --> 00:31:43,040
what made things
spiral out of control.

515
00:31:48,480 --> 00:31:49,480
I know he must have...

516
00:31:50,680 --> 00:31:53,180
tucked it away somewhere safe,

517
00:31:55,720 --> 00:31:57,620
but I just can't find it.

518
00:32:03,530 --> 00:32:04,530
Watch your step.

519
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,570
Seong Woo...

520
00:32:19,380 --> 00:32:21,840
was a truly good friend.

521
00:32:24,450 --> 00:32:26,980
If only that hadn't happened...

522
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:31,250
If only he'd kept
his nose out of it.

523
00:32:35,890 --> 00:32:36,890
Is that why...

524
00:32:38,760 --> 00:32:40,060
you killed him?

525
00:32:42,830 --> 00:32:45,170
No...

526
00:32:46,670 --> 00:32:47,700
I had...

527
00:32:49,010 --> 00:32:52,440
I had no choice. No...

528
00:33:23,170 --> 00:33:26,940
(A Trap Called Desire)

529
00:33:27,110 --> 00:33:28,850
You can tell me everything.

530
00:33:28,950 --> 00:33:31,780
After all, I'm one
of your guardians now, So Yeon.

531
00:33:31,780 --> 00:33:34,850
What is this, a ticking time bomb?

532
00:33:34,950 --> 00:33:36,390
You murdered my father.

533
00:33:36,790 --> 00:33:38,820
Were you really that terrified
of getting caught?

534
00:33:38,920 --> 00:33:39,920
Kang Young Hoon.

535
00:33:40,090 --> 00:33:41,960
What on earth are you hiding?

536
00:33:41,960 --> 00:33:44,690
What are you hiding that you'd go
so far as to pretend to be my mom?

537
00:33:44,760 --> 00:33:45,900
Are we getting another freeloader?

538
00:33:45,960 --> 00:33:49,570
This new guest seems a bit off.

539
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:51,500
Does giving birth make you a mom?

540
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:54,070
Then you shouldn't have switched
Eun Seol and me in the first place.

541
00:33:54,270 --> 00:33:57,410
Eun Seol, isn't your birthday
September 11, too?

542
00:33:57,740 --> 00:34:00,180
What's Hae Ra's blood type?

543
00:34:01,540 --> 00:34:03,550
(Subtitles are provided by KOCOWA.)
